ceipts were up $7.5 billion, nonwithheld receipts were up $3.4 billion, and refunds were down $0.9 billion. The overall increase in receipts is consistent with the increase in personal income over the same period for 1988.\nCorporate Income taxes.--Net corporate receipts for the fourth quarter of fiscal 1989 totaled $23.4 billion, which was $0.2 billion lower than the preceding year. Gross receipts were down $1 billion, reflecting lower corporate profits. This $1 billion decrease was composed of a fall in estimated and final payments of $0.2 billion and $0.8 billion, respectively. Offsetting this fall in gross receipts was an $0.8 billion decrease in corporate refunds.","stderr":"","exit_code":0},"isError":false}}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
